node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
test-results/
playwright-report/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The heavy originals every model in public/models is lightened from. They are the source of
# truth and they are kept, but they are 361 MB and nothing serves them: the game loads the light
# copy beside them. Same argument as the card art below - a blob committed once stays in history
# forever, and on a public repository every clone pays for it. Guarded by
# tests/unit/licensing-boundary.test.ts.
public/models/heavy/

# The models themselves. They live in a Hugging Face repo, named with every file's size and hash in
# models.lock.json, and `npm run models` brings them down into this folder: every version ever
# committed stays in every clone, and they were nearly all of this repository's weight. Guarded by
# tests/unit/models-lock.test.ts.
public/models/*.glb
public/models/*.gltf
public/models/*.part

# Card illustrations fetched by tools/download-card-art.mjs from a third-party
# mirror. They are Critical Role artwork, NOT SRD content: the DPCGL licenses
# the System Reference Document's text and mechanics and does not cover
# illustrations, so nothing here licenses these files for redistribution.
# Fetch them locally, never commit them - a blob committed once stays in
# history forever and only a history rewrite removes it.
# See AGENTS.md, and tests/unit/licensing-boundary.test.ts which guards this.
public/cards/

# Content packs exported by tools/export-pack.ts. The vendored catalogue goes out as one
# importable pack so that deleting the sources loses nothing -- but an export is for whoever
# holds the rights to it, not for the repository to ship. Same reasoning as the card art above:
# what is committed here is the engine, not a catalogue packaged for import. Anchored to the root:
# `public/packs/` is the engine's own pack, written here and shipped with the build.
/packs/

# graft's local graph cache — regenerable, not committed (run `graft build`).
/graft/
